# a release date asserts a publication that did not happen. Both fields are
# added at the moment the release is actually cut, alongside the tag.
#
# `license` names the code licence. Non-code fixtures and documentation are
# CC BY 4.0; imported or executable schemas are Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE-DATA).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use OperateBench, please cite it using the metadata in this file, and
  state the operation_version, engine_version and content digests your run
  artefact recorded (see docs/VERSIONING.md).
title: "OperateBench"
abstract: >-
  OperateBench evaluates whether an agent can keep a persistent business
  operation safe and progressing while time, actors, evidence, authoritative
  systems and external events change independently of the agent. It is a
  deterministic, replayable benchmark in which the execution unit is one
  business operation spanning many agent invocations, with simulated event
  time, first-class WAIT, actor authority and provenance, typed human
  checkpoints, reopen and guarded finality, and an operation-level result
  vector including Human Load. It is a technical preview: one synthetic
  operation, deterministic agents and no published benchmark model results.
type: software
